{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["בלא עת נדתה — after the days of her menstrual impurity. As explained in tractate Niddah: a woman is not called a zavah requiring a sacrifice until after the seven days of menstruation — whether she sees three consecutive days within the eleven days, whether at their beginning or at their end, she requires seven clean days consecutive and a sacrifice on the eighth."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:51.657322376Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}